# Embedded C style for logue SDK

## Naming

- Functions: `snake_case`
- Types: `snake_case_t` or `PascalCase` (match SDK style: `user_osc_param_t`)
- Macros: `UPPER_SNAKE`
- Globals: prefix with `g_`
- Static file-scope: prefix with `s_`

## Safety rules (MISRA-C inspired)

- Every function must have an explicit return type.
- No recursion.
- All loops must have a statically bounded upper limit.
- Pointers must be null-checked before dereference (except SDK-guaranteed pointers).
- `volatile` required for any variable modified in an ISR.
- ISRs must be as short as possible — no DSP processing in ISRs.
- No dynamic memory allocation.
- No `goto` except for a single cleanup label at function end.

## Formatting

- 2-space indentation.
- Braces on same line (`if (x) { ... }`).
- Max line length: 100 characters.
- One blank line between functions.

## Comments

- Use `//` for inline, `/* */` for block.
- Every public function must have a doc comment describing:
  - What it does
  - Parameters (name and meaning)
  - Return value
  - Any real-time constraints
